      from the parsed/interpolated `mcpServerConfig`. Drift is detected
      by structural comparison: string equality on `command`,
      element-by-element equality on `args` (same length, same value
      at every position). Any deviation is drift; matching values are
      not."
    - >-
      "Any null entry in the parsed `mcpServerConfig.args` returns
      `no-mcp-entry`. Detection is a structural property of the parsed
      config — the detector does not pattern-match string contents,
      does not recognize literal sentinels (no `<BRAIN_PATH>`, no
      `<API_TOKEN>`, no magic UUIDs, no sentinel-shaped strings), and
      does not introspect arg semantics. YAML null is the unambiguous
      unwired-slot signal: a bare `-` in `mcpServerConfig.args` parses
      to JS `null`, and that JS `null` triggers `no-mcp-entry`. Null
      in any arg position means the launch command is unwireable, and
      an unwireable launch command means the brain's MCP entry is not
      yet wired — which is exactly what `no-mcp-entry` already means."
    - >-
