      Drift is structural — comparison happens on the in-memory parsed
      entry shape, not on raw text. A user who reformatted their
      `.mcp.json` (different whitespace, key order, trailing newlines)
      without changing the brain entry's `command` or `args` must NOT
      produce a `mcp-drift` result."
    - >-
      "Reading `.mcp.json` before parsing brain.aide. The pipeline
      order encodes the source-of-truth direction: brain.aide is
      canonical, `.mcp.json` is derived. Reading `.mcp.json` first
      inverts that and treats the host's wiring file as authoritative
      ahead of the user's declared config."
    - >-
